{
  "title": "CHAPTER 7: INFLATION & BUSINESS CYCLE",
  "order": 5,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "wle3whv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART 1: INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Inflation is a sustained rise in general price level that decreases purchasing power, measured via CPI and WPI.",
        "RBI targets CPI inflation at 4% ± 2% using monetary tools like Repo Rate, CRR, SLR, and open market operations.",
        "The Short-Run Phillips Curve shows an inverse relationship between inflation and unemployment, while the Long-Run curve is vertical at the Natural Rate of Unemployment.",
        "Stagflation occurs when high inflation, high unemployment, and low growth coexist simultaneously, contradicting the traditional Phillips Curve.",
        "Demand-pull inflation shifts the Aggregate Demand curve right, whereas cost-push inflation shifts the Aggregate Supply curve left."
      ],
      "id": "o4oegy8"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "RBI CPI Target",
          "value": "4% ± 2%",
