    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Inflation refers to a sustained rise in the general price level of goods and services over a period of time. It reduces the purchasing power of money.",
      "id": "5j3dn0j"
    },
    {
      "id": "y97x9th",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. TYPES OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "nug546r",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Demand-Pull Inflation</p>",
            "<p>Demand exceeds supply</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cost-Push Inflation</p>",
            "<p>Rise in production costs</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Creeping Inflation</p>",
            "<p>Slow and steady rise</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Galloping Inflation</p>",
            "<p>Rapid price rise</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hyperinflation</p>",
            "<p>Extremely high inflation</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tccdzvh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. CAUSES OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Increase in money supply<br/>• Excess demand<br/>• Rising wages<br/>• Increase in fuel prices<br/>• Supply shocks<br/>",
      "id": "q8geov6"
    },
    {
      "id": "5isa141",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. EFFECTS OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Decreases purchasing power<br/>• Affects fixed income groups<br/>• Creates uncertainty<br/>• Encourages speculation<br/>",
      "id": "1u0p0jx"
    },
    {
      "id": "4pc3by4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4. CONTROL OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Monetary Measures:<br/>• Increase Repo Rate<br/>• Increase CRR &amp; SLR<br/>• Sell government securities<br/><br/>Fiscal Measures:<br/>• Reduce government expenditure<br/>• Increase taxes<br/>",
      "id": "m6uo1k5"
    },
    {
      "id": "ragig12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5. MEASUREMENT OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Inflation is measured through:<br/>• Consumer Price Index (CPI)<br/>• Wholesale Price Index (WPI)<br/>",
      "id": "f3zfkvu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "RBI targets CPI inflation (4% ± 2%).",
      "id": "qdj161h"
    },
    {
      "id": "69dm1ec",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART 2: BUSINESS CYCLE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Business Cycle refers to periodic fluctuations in economic activity.",
      "id": "uf420oz"
    },
    {
      "id": "9w4ywzw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. PHASES OF BUSINESS CYCLE"
