          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Stagflation is a situation where the economy experiences high inflation, high unemployment, and low economic growth simultaneously.",
      "id": "sgxfzb2"
    },
    {
      "id": "ny4fzaj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. CAUSES OF BUSINESS CYCLE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Changes in investment<br/>• Credit expansion or contraction<br/>• Technological changes<br/>• External shocks<br/>",
      "id": "0nuz7sk"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ado2d6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. CONTROL OF BUSINESS CYCLE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "During Recession:<br/>• Lower interest rates<br/>• Increase public spending<br/><br/>During Inflationary Boom:<br/>• Raise interest rates<br/>• Reduce money supply",
      "id": "c8h1xo0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>PART 3 : ADVANCED INFLATION CONCEPTS</strong>",
      "id": "wwyq035"
    },
    {
      "id": "md90309",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>PHILLIPS CURVE</strong>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Phillips Curve shows the inverse relationship between inflation and unemployment in the short run. When unemployment decreases, inflation tends to rise, and vice versa.",
      "id": "kqoc7u2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Short-Run Phillips Curve:",
      "id": "m402nhe"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Downward sloping curve.<br/>• Low unemployment → High inflation.<br/>• High unemployment → Low inflation.",
      "id": "z2dwnq1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Long-Run Phillips Curve:",
      "id": "md99nwp"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Headline Inflation",
        "Core Inflation"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Scope",
          "Includes all goods and services in the economy",
          "Excludes volatile items from the basket"
        ],
        [
          "Volatile Components",
          "Includes Food and Fuel",
          "Excludes Food and Fuel"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "805igyn"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Vertical at Natural Rate of Unemployment.<br/>• No long-term trade-off between inflation and unemployment.",
      "id": "jxwk5y8"
    },
    {
      "id": "cpkzpvw",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Run</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Relationship</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Short Run</p>",
            "<p>Inverse relationship</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Long Run</p>",
            "<p>No trade-off (Vertical curve)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "i2dfqk0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. STAGFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Stagflation is a situation where the economy experiences high inflation, high unemployment, and low economic growth simultaneously.",
      "id": "zjhgw1l"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It contradicts the traditional Phillips Curve concept.",
      "id": "a7d588p"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Major Cause:<br/>• Supply shocks (e.g., oil crisis of 1970s)<br/>• Increase in production costs<br/>",
      "id": "hastxe4"
    },
    {
      "id": "hgyp8ip",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Indicator</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Condition in Stagflation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Inflation</p>",
            "<p>High</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Unemployment</p>",
            "<p>High</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mwz5md2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. CORE vs HEADLINE INFLATION"
    },
