    {
      "id": "fkrdhg6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. DEMAND-SUPPLY GRAPH EXPLANATION OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Demand-Pull Inflation (Graph Explanation):",
      "id": "d2exnjl"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Core inflation excludes volatile items like food and fuel, while Headline inflation includes all items.",
        "Demand-pull inflation shifts the Aggregate Demand (AD) curve right; Cost-push inflation shifts the Aggregate Supply (AS) curve left.",
        "The Long-Run Phillips Curve is vertical at the Natural Rate of Unemployment.",
        "During a recession, central banks lower interest rates and governments increase public spending to stimulate the economy."
      ],
      "id": "x2gjqyg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Initial equilibrium at intersection of AD and AS.<br/>• Increase in Aggregate Demand shifts AD curve right.<br/>• New equilibrium at higher price level.<br/>",
      "id": "ra6ggtd"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Cost-Push Inflation (Graph Explanation):",
      "id": "3fumxwi"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Increase in production cost shifts AS curve left.<br/>• Price level increases.<br/>• Output decreases.",
      "id": "jpngdva"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Graph Axes Explanation:",
      "id": "jvrivfi"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• X-axis → Output (GDP)<br/>• Y-axis → Price Level<br/>",
      "id": "d8teg8j"
    },
    {
      "id": "jcoxuh6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "RRB HIGH-VALUE EXAM POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Phillips Curve – Short run trade-off exists.<br/>• Long-run Phillips Curve is vertical.<br/>• Stagflation = High inflation + High unemployment.<br/>• Core inflation excludes food &amp; fuel.<br/>• Demand-pull shifts AD right; Cost-push shifts AS left.",
      "id": "5upmegu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Inflation reduces purchasing power<br/>• CPI used for inflation targeting<br/>• Phases: Expansion → Peak → Recession → Depression<br/>• RBI controls inflation through monetary tools<br/>",
      "id": "d4fvktl"
    }
  ],
